  "beginSection": "Begin",
  "introReading": "Complete the Words: type the missing letters to finish each word. Read in Daily Life and Read an Academic Passage: answer the questions about each text; the text stays on screen. You can go back and change answers within this module, and mark questions to revisit.",
  "introListening": "Each recording plays once, then its questions appear one by one. Notes are allowed. Choose a Response: hear one line and pick the best reply. Then conversations, announcements and short academic talks. You cannot go back in Listening.",
  "introBas": "Build a Sentence: for each short exchange, tap the word groups in the right order to make the reply. Tap a placed group to take it back. One group may not belong. About 6 minutes for 10 sentences.",
  "introEmail": "Write an Email: read the situation and write an email that does all three things listed. Use a greeting and a closing, and match your tone to the reader. 7 minutes; about 100-150 words is a good length. There is no spell-check.",
  "introDiscussion": "Write for an Academic Discussion: read the professor's question and two students' posts, then post your own opinion with reasons and an example. Add something new to the discussion. 10 minutes; at least 100 words.",
  "introRepeat": "Listen and Repeat: you will hear a short scenario, then 7 sentences one at a time. After each sentence the microphone turns on: repeat it exactly. The sentences get longer.",
  "introInterview": "Take an Interview: an interviewer asks 4 questions about one topic. After each question you have 45 seconds to answer. There is no preparation time; start speaking when the microphone turns on.",
  "introAdaptive": "This first module is of medium difficulty. How you do here decides whether the second module is easier or harder; only the harder module opens the top bands (5-6).",
  "introSound": "Turn your volume up and use headphones. Recordings are read by your phone's English voice; if you hear nothing, install or update the English voice in your phone's text-to-speech settings.",
